{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310865,"nonce":"5S8bCW4JHhadbKZank9EUuDD9PA=","title":"haxe.Template chain 2026-09-12: seven more links landed (untyped params, string for-in, Null\u003cheap enum\u003e, anon shape ids, List import ...","message":"**STATE (2026-09-12, after 5723a508):** Template runs `plain text`, `::var::`,\n`::if x::` (true) end to end. Conformance 518 -\u003e 522, LOST 0, Haxe suite\n204/0 (+ the 1 nue model crash), fixtures 15/16 (RuntimeMetadata pre-existing).\n\n**LINKS LANDED THIS SESSION, in the order they were exposed:**\n6. `for (c in string)` was UNHANDLED — fell to the ARRAY path and read the\n   string's bytes as elements (fault bytes were the literal text `\"x \"`).\n   `for_in.rs`: `SeqKind::{Array,String}` + `haxe_string_char_code_at_ptr`.\n7. `Optional` arm in the FieldAccess type walk (infer.rs) — was held back\n   as 96d471e; landed.\n8. `infer_return_type_from_body` prefers the first INFORMATIVE return site\n   (a1c9e89); `Null\u003cheap enum\u003e` is the enum's own i64, not a box (types.rs\n   `enum_is_boxed` gate) — an Int box's tag 3 == OpStr's index 3 made the\n   switch \"match\" with an empty payload.\n9. **Unannotated params from CALL uses** (classes.rs\n   `infer_unannotated_param_types`, fixpoint over the class, stored in\n   `inferred_param_types` so the pre-registered signature and the body\n   AGREE). The old field-store recovery was ORDER-SENSITIVE: same-class\n   caller ABOVE the callee got garbage (`-1088528880`). `makeExpr(l)` was\n   the Template shape. **THIS LINK REGRESSED binarytrees 7x** (the pre-pass\n   ran before the class's own fields existed, so ctor params went Dynamic);\n   fixed 2790c89b by lowering fields before functions — see\n   [[feedback_check_ci_benchmarks_after_typer_changes]].\n10. `refine_generic_receiver_from_call` binds through the FORMAL's declaring\n    class (`declared_param_count_of`) because `import haxe.ds.List` resolved\n    to a PLACEHOLDER symbol (566) with no type params and no methods — the\n    typedef `List` in List.hx took the root slot and the class lowered onto\n    the typedef's symbol (52). Stopgap: lower_class_declaration registers the\n    reused symbol under its package. Debt issue 0b91874.\n11. **Anon shape ids collided ACROSS MODULES**: `next_anon_shape_id` was a\n    per-HirToMirContext counter, and the runtime keeps the FIRST descriptor\n    per id — a user `{foo:\"x\"}` reported fields `[l,p,s]` (Template's Token).\n    Now `anon_shape_id(key)` = FNV of the sorted field names, runtime tables\n    are maps (runtime/anon_object.rs, runtime-wasm/lib.rs).\n12. `using` on a Dynamic receiver takes only an extension whose FIRST PARAM\n    is Dynamic (Haxe's `using_field` rule): `d.stringify()` -\u003e Json, but\n    `d.iterator()` must NOT become `StringTools.iterator(d)`. Then E0801\n    (ambiguous dynamic dispatch) is a RUNTIME THROW at the call site instead\n    of failing the whole module (`throw_unresolved_dynamic_call`), so\n    Template compiles; Issue10834/3071 moved COMPILE_FAIL -\u003e CRASH into the\n    same Dynamic-array hole. The throw statement's `stack` population now\n    uses the non-erroring `resolve_field_index_candidates` (E0803 on\n    `throw (e:Eof)` failed haxe.io.Input entirely).\n\n**TRAPS FOUND ON THE WAY:**\n- The call-boundary Dynamic-\u003econcrete unbox (signatures.rs) must be SCALAR\n  ONLY: a Dynamic-typed HIR expr can hold a RAW pointer (an inlined call's\n  result) and `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr` reads its header — 3 suite tests\n  (DebugChecksum, mandelbrot_small) crashed at fault=0x8 until restricted.\n  Conformance alone did NOT show it; the suite did (again).\n- `[mono] ... EXPLICIT type_args` on an import means SPECIALISED = the\n  erased return comes back RAW; the runtime unboxer misreads an enum's tag\n  (0..5) as a box tag. Only bit because the receiver had `type_args: []`.\n- `RAYZOR_SYM_DEBUG=1` prints `import-placeholder \u003cqn\u003e` — the tell for a\n  class resolving to an empty stub.\n- `run_haxe_tests.sh` REBUILDS target/release/rayzor with default features\n  (adds lsp): never juggle stashes while it runs.\n\n**NEXT WALL (issue c911bde, priority:high):** a Dynamic holding an ARRAY:\n`d.length`, `d.hasNext`, `Reflect.field(d, ..)` crash (TRYV3/DYNF probes,\ncrash at HEAD too). Arrays box with RAW TAST ids — `runtime_type_id` has no\nArray arm, TYPE_ARRAY(7) is unused. Fix = box arrays with 7, give the `Array`\nclass symbol id 7, make dynamic field reads consult the tag, then switch the\nE0801 site on the tag. Then `::foreach::` (Issue5293, Issue9372) and the\n`::if::`-false / `(n \u003e 2)` closure defects (424f4d1).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_template_chain_links_6_to_12` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}